    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef pearson(a, b):\n    a = np.asarray(a, dtype=float)\n    b = np.asarray(b, dtype=float)\n    da, db = a - a.mean(), b - b.mean()\n    return round(float((da @ db) / np.sqrt((da @ da) * (db @ db))), 4)\n\nprint(pearson([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [2, 4, 5, 4, 5]))\nprint(pearson([1, 2, 3], [3, 2, 1]))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef pearson(a, b):\n    a = np.asarray(a, dtype=float)\n    b = np.asarray(b, dtype=float)\n    da, db = a - a.mean(), b - b.mean()\n    return round(float((da @ db) / np.sqrt((da @ da) * (db @ db))), 4)\n\nprint(pearson([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [2, 4, 5, 4, 5]))\nprint(pearson([1, 2, 3], [3, 2, 1]))\n```"
